Installing OpenABL from Android (needs root)

1. Copy this openabl folder from the SD card to the top level of Android's
   internal storage.
2. As root, run backup_abl.sh from that folder. It saves your current
   bootloader, so you can always go back to it.
3. Then, as root, run flash_abl.sh to install OpenABL.
4. Turn the handheld off, with the Steamling card still in (the device model
   list comes from the card). Hold Volume Down while turning it on to open the
   OpenABL menu. Volume Up and Down move, Power selects.
5. Set these three:
     Boot mode    -> Linux
     Boot source  -> SD card (or Auto)
     Device model -> your handheld (for example Retroid Pocket 6)
   Don't skip Device model. Without one, OpenABL won't start Steamling and
   drops you straight back into this menu.
6. Pick Start.

If it comes back to the menu, the top line says why ("Start Linux came back:
..."), and the Log entry has the details. docs/install.md in the Steamling repo
has a table of what each message means.
